  <section class="quickstart" id="quick-start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Quick start</h2>
      <!-- The snippet carries the real tile URL rather than hiding it behind a
           "built-in provider", because the URL is the product: it is what this
           site serves, and seeing it is what makes the integration obvious. -->
      <p class="sub">Two steps to a map on screen. Point the engine at our tile servers, and that is the integration. The tiles are public: no key and no sign-up.</p>

      <div class="qs-grid">
        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-step"><span class="n">1</span> Add the package</div>
          <div class="qs-url">
            <code id="pkgUrl">https://github.com/artembobkin/ImmersiveMap.git</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" id="copyPkg" type="button">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p class="qs-hint">In Xcode: <b>File → Add Package Dependencies…</b>, paste the URL, then add the <b>ImmersiveMap</b> library to your app target.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-step"><span class="n">2</span> Drop it into a view</div>
<pre class="qs-pre"><code><span class="k">import</span> SwiftUI
<span class="k">import</span> ImmersiveMap

<span class="k">struct</span> <span class="t">ContentView</span>: <span class="t">View</span> {
    <span class="k">var</span> body: <span class="k">some</span> <span class="t">View</span> {
        <span class="t">ImmersiveMapView</span>()
            .<span class="f">tileURLTemplate</span>(<span class="s">"https://immersivemap.dev/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.mvt"</span>)
            .<span class="f">ignoresSafeArea</span>()
    }
}</code></pre>
          <p class="qs-hint">It renders on iOS and macOS from the same SwiftUI code. The URL above is the whole integration: the planet, z0 to z16, refreshed from OpenStreetMap by our own pipeline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="qs-req">
        <span>Swift 6 · Xcode 16 · iOS 18 · macOS 15</span>
        <a href="/tutorials/">Watch the tutorials →</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/artembobkin/ImmersiveMap#readme">Read the docs →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

